Author: Ronny Kaiser <ronny.kaiser@wandelbots.com>
Date:   Mon Mar 2 09:30:00 2026 +0100

    fix(motion): restore motion after auto-resume and normalize IO polling rate

    TrajectoryExecutor now stores lastAppliedTarget_ and calls
    player_->setTarget() on auto-resume so the time scaling profile
    restarts after brake-to-standstill. Without this, the player
    remains stopped and the executor terminates with MOTION_ENDED.

    Set virtual robot IO polling rate to 200ms (same as physical robots)
    to prevent GCI mutex starvation from continuous listIOValues calls.

